# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# /mixedtape is the shareable name for the record — the link that gets
# sent to someone so they can hear it. The file is mixedtape.html, and
# Pages serves it at /mixedtape on its own: it strips .html and 308s the
# extension form to the clean path. So the canonical URL needs no rule
# here at all.
#
# That 308 is worth knowing, because an earlier attempt fought it and
# lost. /music was a 200 rewrite onto /mixtape.html, and Pages'
# extension-stripping runs BEFORE _redirects — so the rewrite resolved
# to the file, then Pages bounced the browser to /mixtape and the
# address bar showed a name nobody had chosen. Let the platform own the
# clean URL; only name the aliases here.
#
# Everything below is a name the record has answered to at some point.
# Each one 301s to the canonical rather than quietly serving a second
# copy of the same page: one record, one address, however you arrived.
/music          /mixedtape   301
/music.html     /mixedtape   301
/mixtape        /mixedtape   301
/mixtape.html   /mixedtape   301
